<title>SWEDEN: Incentive posts higher 9 month profits.</title>
<headline>Incentive posts higher 9 month profits.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish industrial group Incentive reports for the nine months ending September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items excl ass cos	 3,141 vs   1,963</p>
<p> Profit after fin items incl ass cos	 4,360 vs   3,131</p>
<p> Sales						14,217 vs  17,792</p>
<p> EPS (SKR)					   35.20 vs   22.65</p>
<p> Operating margin (pct)			   24.9 vs    13.9</p>
<p> Operating expenses				9,732 vs  14,462</p>
<p> Profit before deprec			    4,485 vs   3,330</p>
<p> Depreciation					  950 vs     860</p>
<p> Profit after deprec			     3,535 vs   2,470</p>
<p> Net fin items				CHARGE 394 vs     507 CH</p>
<p> Share in earnings of associated cos	 1,219 vs   1,168</p>
<p> Tax						   1,848 vs   1,162</p>
<p> Minorities				   CHARGE 105 vs     420 CH</p>
<p> Net profit					  2,407 vs   1,549</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full company name is Incentive AB.</p>
<p>*= exceptional income of 2,570 million crowns for sale of shares and companies and amortisation for goodwill concening the acquisition of Gambro against 474 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
